# XSH feholdexcept()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Every exception and rounding macro is optional (XBD <fenv.h>): a test that
# uses one is NOTINUSE when it is not defined, or when fewer than two
# rounding directions can be selected.

assertion  XSH.feholdexcept.001
anchor     functions/feholdexcept.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/feholdexcept.html#RETURN VALUE
class      disputed
since      2001
says       feholdexcept() returns zero (it returns zero only if a non-stop mode
           was installed).
note       disputed (Q-110): the page asks for a non-stop mode only "if
           available" and does not say whether an implementation may lack one,
           so a nonzero return cannot be called a failure; the test is
           UNRESOLVED for it. The tests of the other behaviours do the same.
test       t/001-return.c

assertion  XSH.feholdexcept.002
anchor     functions/feholdexcept.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       The environment saved by feholdexcept() includes the rounding
           direction: after it is changed, fesetenv() with the saved
           environment reinstates the direction in force at the call.
test       t/002-saves-env.c

assertion  XSH.feholdexcept.003
anchor     functions/feholdexcept.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       When feholdexcept() returns, every exception flag is clear.
test       t/003-clears-flags.c

assertion  XSH.feholdexcept.004
anchor     functions/feholdexcept.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       The saved environment holds the flags that were set before the call:
           fesetenv() with it raises them again.
test       t/004-saves-flags.c

assertion  XSH.feholdexcept.005
anchor     functions/feholdexcept.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       After feholdexcept() has returned zero, each defined exception
           raised by an arithmetic operation is recorded in the flags and the
           program continues (non-stop mode).
test       t/005-non-stop.c
